  "id": "vasopressor",
  "term": "vasopressor",
  "definition": "A vasopressor is a medication used in shock or other hemodynamically unstable states to help stabilize a critically ill patient. In the source, it is discussed as a treatment that may be started through a peripheral line early, as a temporary measure before transfer or before central venous access is available.",
